<title>FRANCE: EU adds 300,000 tonnes to Spain maize import quota.</title>
<headline>EU adds 300,000 tonnes to Spain maize import quota.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday raised an allocation for preferential maize imports to Spain by 300,000 tonnes, French cereals office ONIC said.</p>
<p>The previous allocation was 500,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Under a trade agreement with the United States, traders can bid for reductions in import tariffs up to a set quantity of maize available at a tender.</p>
<p>Bidding for tariff reductions under the previous quota of 500,000 tonnes began on Thursday but the EU's cereals management committee rejected all bids, officials said earlier.</p>
<p>The preferential imports are designed to compensate United States farmers for trade losses caused by Spain's accession to the EU in 1986.</p>
</text>
